  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 205 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nAbove-normal temperatures will likely continue through at least \nThursday as bias-corrected probabilistic guidance indicates little\ntemperature spread with even the 10th percentile above-normal\nthrough that period. High temperatures will range from the mid \n90s to the low 100s deg F.\n\nEnsemble spread increases among the global models by late in the \nweek into next weekend (September 18-20), which indicates the \npotential for a pattern change. There is a chance the subtropical \nridge will break down as a mid-level trough digs across the\nPlains. This would drive a cold front southward into the Southern\nPlains. There is a 30 to 70% chance of high temperatures below 90\ndeg F by Saturday (30% southeast; 70% north). The coldest end of \nguidance indicates a low to medium chance (5% southeast; 50% \nnorth) of high temperatures below 80 deg F. These probabilities \nincrease by 10 to 20% by Sunday (i.e., the chance of cooler\nweather increases later in the weekend).\n\nMahale",
